.TH PATCHMGR 1 "February 2026" "PatchMgr 2.1.0" "System Administration"

.SH NAME
patchmgr \- Linux Patch Management Automation Tool

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patchmgr
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
PatchMgr is a modular Linux patch automation tool designed to perform
pre-checks, apply updates, validate system state, and generate reports.

It provides interactive and non-interactive patching modes with logging,
reboot detection, and dry-run capabilities.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B precheck
Run pre-patch validation checks including uptime, disk usage, memory usage,
and failed services.

.TP
.B apply
Apply available system updates.

.TP
.B postcheck
Run post-patch validation checks including kernel version and failed services.

.TP
.B report
Generate a patch summary report.

.TP
.B full
Run the complete patch lifecycle:
precheck → apply → postcheck → report.

.TP
.B version
Display the PatchMgr version.

.TP
.B help
Display usage information.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Automatically confirm patching and reboot actions without prompting.

.TP
.B --dry-run
Simulate patching without making changes. Shows upgradable packages only.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/patchmgr/
Directory where patch logs and reports are stored.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.

.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.

